# How to write useful apps with Wolfram & WLJS, or swimming against the stream
Everyone knows a million ways to write an app with Node (or Bun, but technically it is still JavaScript), Java, or Python. Any "adult" language—C/C++, C#, Pascal/Delphi, and many others—offers tons of options to choose from. But what about our symbolic friend Wolfram?<br /><br />

## The Answer
There is no way. Wolfram cannot be compiled into a binary; Mathematica costs a lot for a team, and it is slow and unstable when it comes to building UIs. CDF Player (Pro) is deprecated and subscription-based. Just use Claude Code with Bun, or Codex, or Kirbi; throw the rest into the garbage bin and vibe.


![](/attachments/image-5df.png)

